<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">14th Dalai Lama</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1935</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Tenzin Gyatso</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The 14th <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalai-lama">Dalai Lama</a>, Tenzin Gyatso, was born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amdo">Amdo</a> and recognised as the reincarnation of the Thirteenth Dalai Lama, being enthroned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lhasa">Lhasa</a> in 1940. He took full power in 1950 as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-liberation-army">People's Liberation Army</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>. After the failed uprising of 1959 he fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and set up a government in exile at Dharamsala. He received the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> in 1989.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/14th-dalai-lama.jpg" alt="14th Dalai Lama" width="320" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Niccolò Caranti · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tenzin_Gyatso_-_Trento_2013_01.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
